    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>Gather more data ;-)  Or if you have prior beliefs justified by strong theory and/or prior empirical evidence, you can use informative priors in blavaan to overcome the lack of information in your data.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/resources.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/resources.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422847343000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_Ocd9e1uBnkXTvMTg8IFf\">https://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/resources.html</a><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Does anyone know what Lavaan can handle if nobs &lt; nvar</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>What do you mean &quot;handle&quot;?  It was only a warning, so it sounds like the optimizer still might have found a solution against all odds.  But it doesn&#39;t follow that you can place a lot of faith in the solution, since you are essentially trying to model more information than you actually observed.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422847343000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0oNurECLZ_07OEBFHOXgHi\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ]
